-- expect: 9:46: `f` is a block parameter given an effectful block: it can only be called, or passed on to a block parameter of a call; a block is not stored (SPEC §30)
-- An effectful block stored (SPEC §30): `keep` answers its block parameter. Given a block that
-- awaits, `keep`'s copy at the block's row would hand the block out of the call, where no site of
-- its row need be. A block passed to a function is called there or passed on, never stored or
-- returned; a stored callback is boxed at a bound (§28, docs/async-capabilities.md §2.3).
effect Async { ctl await() }
handler skip[A]: Async, A -> A = { return(v) = v; await(k) = k(()) }

fn keep(f: !(i32 => i32)) -> !(i32 => i32) = f

main -> i32 = with skip { let g = keep(!{ x -> await(); x }); 0 }
